# Recommended LMLM RISC-V setup — zero hardware, low budget

My recommendation is to start with QEMU and FreeBSD 14.5 RISC-V 64-bit, rather than buying a development board immediately.

This gives you a way to investigate the RISC-V architecture, boot FreeBSD, develop system services and test LMLM's execution adapters without spending money on physical hardware.

Recommended starting point: QEMU + FreeBSD

## 1. Your proposed architecture

LMLM Core

Reasoning · Models · Agent orchestration

LMLM RISC-V Adapter

Command interface · RPC · Policy enforcement

QEMU RISC-V 64-bit

Virtual hardware

FreeBSD 14.5

Kernel · Networking · Filesystem · Services

The important architectural decision is to keep LMLM's control plane independent of the operating system running on an execution node.

